%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: DetectiveMonika3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081049
    - rid: 4972359976905081050
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: There's the lake, so we must not be far from whatever it is Anoriath
      saw.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081051
    - rid: 4972359976905081052
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you smell that?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081055
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Something does smell a bit off...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Let's follow our noses, then.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081056
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081057
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Woah...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081058
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Okay, maybe he saw these poor people getting killed?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081060
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: That would mean our suspect would be a serial killer, but why would she
      kill these people?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081061
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: If anyone's going to be involved with murders of the Talos faithful,
      it would be the Thalmor.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081062
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, but aren't they High Elves?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Unless they paid someone off to do the killing for them...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081063
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: That might make sense-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081064
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: When Anoriath goes out hunting, he spots the Thalmor massacring these
      people...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Fearing that he'd tell people what he saw, they hired a killer to take
      care of the problem without drawing any attention to themselves.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081065
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: 'That <i>could</i> explain the red herring of the stab wounds:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081066
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The killer wanted to create as much confusion as possible so that her
      employers don't catch any suspicion.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081067
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: If the Thalmor really are behind this, we shouldn't be here- there's
      no telling what they'll do to us.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081069
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... You think they'd have the guts to have investigators killed?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081070
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: They have access to professional killers; I'd rather live to tell our
      tale.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081071
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I suppose you're right...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081072
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm a bit doubtful that the Thalmor would feel the need to silence Anoriath.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081073
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Why's that?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081074
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: The White-Gold Concordat made Talos worship illegal, after the Markarth
      Incident they pushed for the right to enforce it.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081075
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: As disgusting as it is, they have the legal right to punish those who
      commit the "crime."
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: They conveniently left out the specific punishment, meaning that any
      Justiciar could do whatever they want if they so much as see an amulet of Talos.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: So why would they feel the need to hide their involvement?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Maybe if we learn more about the people who were killed at the shrine,
      we'll find out why they felt the need to cover it up.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081076
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: Very well, captain-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081077
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: If it isn't the Captain of the Guard of Whiterun. What brings you to
      this neck of the woods?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081078
    - rid: 4972359976905081079
    - rid: 4972359976905081082
    - rid: 4972359976905081083
    - rid: 4972359976905081084
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: Surely you're not merely on patrol, this territory is under the jurisdiction
      of Falkreath hold, no?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081080
    - rid: 4972359976905081081
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: And I doubt you have the luxury of time to go on a... romantic walk.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: The Thalmor Justiciar is accompanied by three Thalmor soldiers.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: My relationship with Ivar is strictly professional.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081085
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Of course it is... But that doesn''t answer my question: why are you
      here?'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081086
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081087
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: To tell you the truth... um...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081088
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: We heard reports of a dragon attack on Falkreath, so Jarl Balgruuf sent
      us to see the damages with our own eyes.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081089
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: ... Does your Jarl really have no one else to send for an inspection
      than guards who should be defending <i>his</i> realm?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081090
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: Of course he'd send us, you'd trust some courier to make it back alive
      if the dragon was still there?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081091
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm... maybe not.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: But <i>we</i> didn't hear any reports of a dragon attacking Falkreath.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081092
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I guess the reports were false, then; some poor farmer must've mistaken
      a big bird for a dragon or something.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081093
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: Ha. You Nords would be stupid enough to waste men on some foolish farmer's
      folly.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081094
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: How lucky it was that we met then, we saved you the trouble of finding
      nothing.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081095
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: You should get back to your Jarl and let him that everything's alright.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081096
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Sure thing-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081097
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 639d4037fbc3acd41947392e6542aac6, type: 2}
    dialog: Monika and Ivar start making their return trip to Whiterun.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, and one last thing-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081098
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 868c924e69c3f334bb0460b9b886366d, type: 2}
    dialog: It isn't wise to lie to your superiors.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081099
    - rid: 4972359976905081100
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081101
    - rid: 4972359976905081102
    - rid: 4972359976905081103
    - rid: 4972359976905081104
    - rid: 4972359976905081105
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Okay, he was totally suspicious of us, which means he's definitely involved.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081106
    - rid: 4972359976905081107
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: If the Thalmor are involved, who can we even get help from?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081108
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: ... I think the highest authority we could refer to would be the Penitus
      Oculatus.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081109
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: They're the emperor's personal bodyguards and spies-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081110
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: So if anyone would have the authority and means to investigate Thalmor
      wrong-doing, it would be them.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Where can we find them?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081111
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: They should have an outpost in Dragon Bridge, up by Solitude.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081112
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: But we really should check in with the Jarl first.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081114
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... yeah, you're right.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972359976905081113
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116224
    - rid: 4972360025000116225
    - rid: 4972360025000116226
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... so based on what we found, we think that the Thalmor are ultimately
      responsible.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116227
    - rid: 4972360025000116229
    - rid: 4972360025000116230
    - rid: 4972360025000116231
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5301facf4ef9bfe46bdb4745494365d2, type: 2}
    dialog: That's...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116232
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5301facf4ef9bfe46bdb4745494365d2, type: 2}
    dialog: Very troublesome.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5301facf4ef9bfe46bdb4745494365d2, type: 2}
    dialog: As I'm sure you're aware, any sign of resistance against the Thalmor
      could be seen as escalatory.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5301facf4ef9bfe46bdb4745494365d2, type: 2}
    dialog: If pushed, the Imperials would likely make any concession they would
      demand; anything to keep the fragile peace intact for one more day.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5301facf4ef9bfe46bdb4745494365d2, type: 2}
    dialog: 'I cannot in good conscience order you to investigate this further; publicly
      declare the murder to be fully the fault of the unknown Dunmer woman. '
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116233
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5301facf4ef9bfe46bdb4745494365d2, type: 2}
    dialog: ... I will say that what you do on your own time is your business, and
      that you don't need to tell me every little detail of your personal affairs.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116234
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I see...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5301facf4ef9bfe46bdb4745494365d2, type: 2}
    dialog: The both of you are dismissed, good work.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: I'm not comfortable with helping you with this further, Captain.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116235
    - rid: 4972360025000116236
    - rid: 4972360025000116237
    - rid: 4972360025000116238
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: If you wish to seek out the Penitus Oculatus, I will have no part of
      it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I understand, besides-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116239
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: It'd be cruel of me to order you to march on that singed leg of yours.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116240
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: If you say so. Stay safe.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116241
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: You too.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116242
    - rid: 4972360025000116244
    - rid: 4972360025000116245
    - rid: 4972360025000116253
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (So the murder plot is a cold war conspiracy now?)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116246
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Wild.)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116247
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (<b>You</b> know if Sayori found {mc} yet?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116248
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116252
    - rid: 4972360025000116254
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4972360025000116255
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
